{"clock":1,"nonce":"32af43e30b99c2c5afb65cf2664e77d4","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792577111,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5958448221"},"data":{"body":"Found in the native-fields final review; it predates native-fields. In both adapters, `confirm()` (bridge/github/remote.go, bridge/gitlab/remote.go) checks the repository after a write or read answers \"not found\". When that check fails too, `confirm()` wraps the original not-found, and the engine marks the bug gone for good: every later pull and push skips it.\n\nFix: when the repository check fails, return its own error, not the not-found, so the bug stays synced and the run reports the failure. Add a test with a reader that can't see the repository.\n","title":"bridge: a failed repository check after a not-found marks a bug gone"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792611712,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5958448221"},"data":{"add":["kind:bug","prio:p2","status:backlog","assignee:guilbep"],"remove":null}}]}